Expected elements: present

Presence, my own verdict: the replay telemetry is PRESENT. `.panebody` is `overflow:auto`, and the Transaction pane paints a bottom fade — measured x1750, #ECECEC to #FFFFFF across y1051-1074 — a treatment that exists only because content overflows. It is a scroll region; `effectsMismatched: 0` is below the fold, not clipped.

That fade spends 24px on 19 luminance levels (0.8/px), so nothing says "more below"; and the telemetry, this page's strongest claim, is ranked last, under DECODED INPUT, SELECTOR, RAW, a paragraph and the JSON block whose first glyph is half-drawn at y1070. No type level, lowest position.

`Supply sources` (x13-119, y287-309) does not read as inert. Its label ink is right (#565656, the muted rung; body prose #484848), but `.btn.disabled` gives it a #DDDDDD body on a #FFFFFF pane — the only filled object in the 909x1003 Code pane, its heaviest mass. Every other inert control here is body-less: the eight stepping controls (x474-536) and the OPENING/POSITIONING segments (x1400-1560) measure white fill, #C8C8C8 hairline, #565656 glyph. The fix inverted the pattern it claimed to match.

Re-tests: hash mid-byte break HOLDS (41 hex glyphs line 1, 23 line 2). ISO hyphen break HOLDS. Fee row HOLDS — label 154px on one line, 51px clear (not 55), row 46px vs 30-32px siblings, break value-side. WITHDRAWN: "nothing grouped" — every other figure is a block height or under 1000.

Fixes: give the inert button the body-less treatment; lift the telemetry above RAW.

Rating: 6/10

